<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mauryas of Konkan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th–8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Mauryas</a> of Konkan were a dynasty that ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the sixth and seventh centuries, claiming descent from the Maurya emperors. Their island capital, Puri, has been identified with Elephanta or a nearby site. They were defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kirtivarman-i">Kirtivarman I</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badami">Badami</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pulakeshin-ii">Pulakeshin II</a> later took Puri with a large fleet.</p></div>
